WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:07.640
House of the Dragon Episode 2 has a dragon
showdown, two awkward marriage proposals,

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:10.780
and the reveal of Craghas Crabfeeder.

00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:13.309
So – what’s going on, and what does it
mean?

00:00:13.309 --> 00:00:17.279
This video has no spoilers beyond Hot D Episode
2.

00:00:17.279 --> 00:00:20.779
It starts with a new opening sequence for
the series.

00:00:20.779 --> 00:00:26.300
It shows a model city, like the one Viserys
makes, but with a stream of blood running

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:27.449
through it.

00:00:27.449 --> 00:00:32.960
This represents the bloodline of House Targaryen
– it’s a family tree showing the last

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:35.800
hundred years of Targaryen kings.

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:40.660
It starts with this image of Valyria, the
old empire of the dragonlords.

00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:50.630
Valyria was destroyed in the mysterious Doom,
but the Targaryens survived by coming to Dragonstone.

00:00:50.630 --> 00:00:55.629
This next image is of Aegon’s Conquest,
when Aegon Targaryen and his sisters and their

00:00:55.629 --> 00:00:57.910
dragons took over Westeros.

00:00:57.910 --> 00:01:03.570
Here, the bloodline splits into two – because
Aegon had one son with his sister-wife Rhaenys,

00:01:03.570 --> 00:01:06.870
and one son with his other sister-wife Visenya.

00:01:06.870 --> 00:01:11.790
The Rhaenys symbol shows a dragon skull with
bolt through the eye – because Rhaenys and

00:01:11.790 --> 00:01:15.300
her dragon were shot down with a scorpion
bolt in Dorne.

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:19.100
Rhaenys’ bloodline continues to her son
King Aenys.

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:25.010
Aegon’s other son Maegor also became king,
but he never had children, and so isn’t

00:01:25.010 --> 00:01:26.470
included in this bloodline.

00:01:26.470 --> 00:01:32.990
After Maegor, Aenys’ son Jaehaerys became
king, and he married his sister Alysanne.

00:01:32.990 --> 00:01:36.300
Here, the bloodline splits into nine streams.

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:41.270
Because Jaehaerys and Alysanne had nine children
who survived to adulthood.

00:01:41.270 --> 00:01:46.390
Next are Jaehaerys’ kids Baelon and Alyssa
– Baelon has a Hand symbol, because Baelon

00:01:46.390 --> 00:01:48.070
was Hand of the King.

00:01:48.070 --> 00:01:51.710
Baelon and Alyssa’s son was King Viserys
– you can recognise his crown symbol.

00:01:51.710 --> 00:01:56.000
Viserys married Aemma Arryn – and she’s
got the Arryn sigil.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:02.150
After Aemma is long stream of blood, which
evokes Aemma’s stillbirths and miscarriages

00:02:02.150 --> 00:02:03.660
and.. her death.

00:02:03.660 --> 00:02:08.130
But then we see her daughter Rhaenyra – with
the symbol of the Valyrian steel necklace

00:02:08.130 --> 00:02:10.620
that Daemon gave her last episode.

00:02:10.620 --> 00:02:15.360
And there’s an image of the ceremony where
Rhaenyra was named heir to the Throne.

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:21.250
Meanwhile, in the background, we see the bloodline
of the Velaryons shown with blue symbols.

00:02:21.250 --> 00:02:26.390
And see the bloodline of Otto Hightower with
the Hand of the King symbol – and his daughter

00:02:26.390 --> 00:02:29.250
Alicent with the Hightower sigil.

00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:35.040
So this new intro is a visual summary of the
Targaryen bloodline alongside the Velaryons

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:36.410
and Hightowers.

00:02:36.410 --> 00:02:40.621
Maybe the intro will change throughout the
season as the family changes – cause this

00:02:40.621 --> 00:02:44.560
season occasionally jumps forward in time
several years.

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:49.721
The blood imagery reminds us that the history
of the royal family is written in the blood

00:02:49.721 --> 00:02:55.380
of birth and the blood of battle, and in a
lot of red wine.

00:02:55.380 --> 00:03:01.290
The bloodline is running downhill, which suggests
the Targaryens are in decline, falling from

00:03:01.290 --> 00:03:06.460
their peak at Valyria down towards fiery disaster.

00:03:06.460 --> 00:03:10.590
The episode starts about six months after
the previous episode.

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:15.530
We see that Craghas Crabfeeder has attacked
another Westerosi ship.

00:03:15.530 --> 00:03:20.410
Crabfeeder is the leader of the Triarchy,
an alliance of eastern cities who have taken

00:03:20.410 --> 00:03:22.990
over the Stepstones islands.

00:03:22.990 --> 00:03:28.370
Craghas is called Crabfeeder because he nails
his enemies to the beach so they get eaten

00:03:28.370 --> 00:03:31.020
alive by crabs.

00:03:31.020 --> 00:03:35.480
According to a behind-the-scenes video, Crabfeeder
has greyscale.

00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:40.910
Greyscale is a disease that slowly turns the
body into stone – we saw stone men infected

00:03:40.910 --> 00:03:46.090
with greyscale in Game of Thrones –Jorah
Mormont catches greyscale.

00:03:46.090 --> 00:03:50.750
Greyscale can eventually cause madness, so
it looks like this disease makes the Crabfeeder

00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:53.390
crazy and dangerous.

00:03:53.390 --> 00:03:58.230
He wears a mask similar to the Sons of the
Harpy mask from Game of Thrones – the idea

00:03:58.230 --> 00:04:04.430
is that Crabfeeder created his outfit from
bits and pieces that he found in shipwrecks.

00:04:04.430 --> 00:04:09.800
Crabfeeder’s attacks are disrupting the
trade that makes Corlys rich.

00:04:09.800 --> 00:04:12.709
So Corlys wants to attack Crabfeeder immediately.

00:04:12.709 --> 00:04:18.789
But King Viserys doesn’t want a big war
– so he sends diplomats to the eastern cities

00:04:18.789 --> 00:04:23.349
of Pentos and Volantis to see if they’ll
help against the Triarchy.

00:04:23.349 --> 00:04:29.110
And this might actually be a smart move – getting
the Free Cities to sort this out amongst themselves

00:04:29.110 --> 00:04:32.080
so the Targaryens don’t have to go to war.

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:35.680
But Corlys says this makes the Targaryens
look weak.

00:04:35.680 --> 00:04:39.970
And Rhaenyra says they should send dragonriders
as a show of force.

00:04:39.970 --> 00:04:45.380
Everyone’s talking back to King Viserys,
and questioning him, but when Rhaenyra speaks

00:04:45.380 --> 00:04:49.599
up, Viserys and Otto shut her down and send
her away.

00:04:49.599 --> 00:04:54.210
Rhaenyra feels frustrated that even though
she’s the heir to the Throne, she’s not

00:04:54.210 --> 00:04:59.789
allowed to participate in politics, she’s
still just the cupbearer, Viserys is still

00:04:59.789 --> 00:05:04.169
treating her like a “little girl”.

00:05:04.169 --> 00:05:08.820
The Commander of the Kingsguard, Ryam Redwyne,
has died of natural causes.

00:05:08.820 --> 00:05:13.919
And there are always seven Kingsguard, so
now they need a new member to replace Ryam.

00:05:13.919 --> 00:05:19.909
Otto chooses candidates from houses Caron,
Mallister, Corbray, Rowan, Crakehall and Tarly

00:05:19.909 --> 00:05:25.210
– House Tarly is the family of Sam and Randyll
in Game of Thrones.

00:05:25.210 --> 00:05:30.809
Each candidate is represented by a carved
model – kinda like the small council balls,

00:05:30.809 --> 00:05:36.750
and Viserys’ dragon statue – suggesting
that everyone here is just a piece in a game..

00:05:36.750 --> 00:05:38.009
of thrones.

00:05:38.009 --> 00:05:44.839
Otto tells Rhaenyra to say polite courtesies
to the knights, so she plays that role, with

00:05:44.839 --> 00:05:47.599
a fake fleeting smile.

00:05:47.599 --> 00:05:53.909
This is what’s expected of young lady – smiles
and courtesies – but Rhaenyra has more to

00:05:53.909 --> 00:05:54.909
offer.

00:05:54.909 --> 00:05:59.300
Otto says they should choose the Mallister
or Crakehall knight for the Kingsguard, because

00:05:59.300 --> 00:06:01.490
those houses are important politically.

00:06:01.490 --> 00:06:08.080
But the Kingsguard are meant to be apolitical
and unbiased, simply the best and most honourable

00:06:08.080 --> 00:06:09.300
knights in the realm.

00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:14.310
But when Kingsguard are chosen for political
reasons instead, that can make the Kingsguard

00:06:14.310 --> 00:06:18.710
weaker – by the time of Game of Thrones,
most of the Kingsguard aren’t great knights

00:06:18.710 --> 00:06:24.080
– they’re corrupt cronies, cowards and
oathbreakers.

00:06:24.080 --> 00:06:29.580
Rhaenyra wants her father’s guards to actually
be great fighters, so she chooses Criston

00:06:29.580 --> 00:06:35.129
Cole, because he has real battle experience
– &lt;and also because he’s hot.

00:06:35.129 --> 00:06:42.400
King Viserys and Alicent have a hang out..
date.. meeting, and Viserys talks about Valyria,

00:06:42.400 --> 00:06:44.939
the old dragonlord empire.

00:06:44.939 --> 00:06:50.750
The Valyrian capital city was built on volcanoes
called the Fourteen Flames – and Viserys

00:06:50.750 --> 00:06:55.229
says the volcanoes were the source of Valyrian
magic and power.

00:06:55.229 --> 00:07:01.729
The books say that “All Valyrian sorcery
was rooted in blood or fire” – their sorcerers

00:07:01.729 --> 00:07:07.580
used glass candles that let them see across
the world, and enter peoples’ dreams.

00:07:07.580 --> 00:07:14.680
Viserys says the Valyrian blood mages lived
in the Anogrion – anogri apparently means

00:07:14.680 --> 00:07:16.770
blood in Valyrian.

00:07:16.770 --> 00:07:22.169
The books say that Valyrian blood mages did
some crazy messed up stuff.

00:07:22.169 --> 00:07:28.259
They twisted the flesh of beasts and men to
create monstrous chimeras.

00:07:28.259 --> 00:07:34.810
In the flesh pits of Gogossos, “beasts were
mated to slave women to bring forth twisted

00:07:34.810 --> 00:07:37.279
half-human children”.

00:07:37.279 --> 00:07:43.289
Some fans theorise that Valyrian blood magic
created dragons, and gave the Targaryens the

00:07:43.289 --> 00:07:46.520
dragon blood that allows them to control dragons.

00:07:46.520 --> 00:07:52.719
In this episode, we see a painting on a wall
of a dragon having sex with humans – the

00:07:52.719 --> 00:07:55.590
blood of the dragon may be literal.

00:07:55.590 --> 00:07:59.159
But Viserys doesn’t mention Valyria’s
blood magic monstrosities.

00:07:59.159 --> 00:08:00.160
[Or that his ancestors might’ve been lizards].

00:08:00.160 --> 00:08:05.059
Or the fact that Valyria’s volcanoes were
full of slaves being worked to death in the

00:08:05.059 --> 00:08:06.410
burning mines.

00:08:06.410 --> 00:08:13.129
It’s crazy how Viserys admires the glory
of Valyria when Valyria was so evil – it’s

00:08:13.129 --> 00:08:17.090
like he’s playing with a Lego model of magic
nasty Germany.

00:08:17.090 --> 00:08:23.999
Viserys and Alicent compare Valyria and its
fall to Westeros, then Viserys drops a statue

00:08:23.999 --> 00:08:29.389
of a dragon – which heavily foreshadows
disaster for the Targaryen dynasty.

00:08:29.389 --> 00:08:34.899
Viserys and Alicent have been having these
meeting/hang/dates for a while.

00:08:34.899 --> 00:08:39.681
On one level, it’s an innocent friendship
– Alicent understands Viserys’ grief for

00:08:39.681 --> 00:08:45.709
his dead wife Aemma, because her own mother
died, so she feels real sympathy for Viserys.

00:08:45.709 --> 00:08:51.220
But at the same time, Alicent visits Viserys
because Otto told her to, he wants her to

00:08:51.220 --> 00:08:55.009
hook up with the king to make the Hightowers
more powerful.

00:08:55.009 --> 00:09:00.579
Alicent’s actor said it’s “ambiguous”
to what extent Alicent is scheming for Otto

00:09:00.579 --> 00:09:02.540
instead of being genuine.

00:09:02.540 --> 00:09:08.029
Ultimately, Alicent is a fourteen year old
girl who has to obey her father and her king

00:09:08.029 --> 00:09:13.319
– and we can see how anxious that makes
her feel when she picks at her fingernails.

00:09:13.319 --> 00:09:17.860
The relationship is further complicated by
Alicent’s friendship with Rhaenyra – cause

00:09:17.860 --> 00:09:23.620
Viserys tells Alicent not to tell Rhaenyra
about their.. meetings, which forces Alicent

00:09:23.620 --> 00:09:28.980
to choose between loyalty to her king and
loyalty to her best friend.

00:09:28.980 --> 00:09:34.410
Alicent and Rhaenyra go to a sept, which a..
church of the Faith of the Seven.

00:09:34.410 --> 00:09:39.029
Alicent is a believer of the Faith – which
makes sense, because her family the Hightowers

00:09:39.029 --> 00:09:41.870
of Oldtown, have close ties with the Faith.

00:09:41.870 --> 00:09:47.769
But Rhaenyra is not so religious – some
Targaryens don’t worship gods, preferring

00:09:47.769 --> 00:09:50.579
to think of themselves as gods.

00:09:50.579 --> 00:09:55.971
So Alicent teaches Rhaenyra to pray at the
statue of the Mother, to feel closer to their

00:09:55.971 --> 00:09:58.160
own dead mothers.

00:09:58.160 --> 00:10:01.040
Alicent and Rhaenyra have a deep bond.

00:10:01.040 --> 00:10:05.910
But when they talk about Viserys remarrying,
Alicent doesn’t tell Rhaenyra about her

00:10:05.910 --> 00:10:07.570
meetings with Viserys.

00:10:07.570 --> 00:10:12.149
So she’s not being completely honest with
her friend.

00:10:12.149 --> 00:10:18.050
Viserys speaks with Lord Corlys and his wife
Rhaenys, who say the Targaryen throne looks

00:10:18.050 --> 00:10:23.900
vulnerable – Crabfeeder has the Stepstones,
Dameon’s on Dragonstone, Queen Aemma is

00:10:23.900 --> 00:10:26.750
dead, and the heir to the throne is a girl.

00:10:26.750 --> 00:10:32.660
Corlys uses a sailing metaphor about facing
a storm, because Corlys is a famous sailor

00:10:32.660 --> 00:10:34.500
who has travelled the world.

00:10:34.500 --> 00:10:40.399
Corlys proposes that King Viserys marry his
daughter Laena, to make the royal family stronger

00:10:40.399 --> 00:10:44.220
by deepening the Targaryen-Velaryon alliance.

00:10:44.220 --> 00:10:50.029
This alliance has been shaky ever since Rhaenys
was rejected at the Harrenhal Council.

00:10:50.029 --> 00:10:56.269
Marrying Laena to the king would bring them
closer, and would make Corlys even more powerful.

00:10:56.269 --> 00:11:01.639
But Viserys is not keen to marry a twelve
year old girl, and he’s still grieving his

00:11:01.639 --> 00:11:08.629
dead wife Aemma, so Viserys appears indecisive
and uncertain – which is really not how

00:11:08.629 --> 00:11:10.279
a king should behave.

00:11:10.279 --> 00:11:15.319
Viserys and Rhaenyra try to talk and connect,
but it’s awkward.

00:11:15.319 --> 00:11:20.310
The silence is highlighted by the sound of
crickets, and by the physical distance between

00:11:20.310 --> 00:11:22.829
Viserys and Rhaenyra at table.

00:11:22.829 --> 00:11:27.230
Rhaenyra brings up the council earlier – she
wants Viserys to listen to what she has to

00:11:27.230 --> 00:11:31.959
say – but Viserys just talks over Rhaenyra
again.

00:11:31.959 --> 00:11:39.000
We see that Viserys’ finger is rotting – after
it was cut on the Iron Throne last episode.

00:11:39.000 --> 00:11:45.850
This is another bad omen hinting that power
is killing Viserys, that the Throne is rejecting

00:11:45.850 --> 00:11:46.850
him.

00:11:46.850 --> 00:11:52.279
The rotting hand also suggests that the Hand
of the King Otto is corrupt.

00:11:52.279 --> 00:11:58.260
Seeing maggots eat his flesh evokes Viserys’
line last episode, about crows feasting on

00:11:58.260 --> 00:12:00.310
his family’s corpses.

00:12:00.310 --> 00:12:07.830
This political world is eating Viserys alive,
and two of the hungriest vultures are Otto

00:12:07.830 --> 00:12:09.050
and Mellos.

00:12:09.050 --> 00:12:13.390
Viserys says that Corlys proposed marriage
to Laena.

00:12:13.390 --> 00:12:17.990
And this worries Otto, cause he wants Viserys
to marry his daughter Alicent.

00:12:17.990 --> 00:12:23.750
Otto shares some knowing looks with Grand
Maester Mellos – it’s obvious that these

00:12:23.750 --> 00:12:25.920
two are working together.

00:12:25.920 --> 00:12:32.050
We saw them conniving in the shadows last
episode, and saw a maester whispering in Otto’s

00:12:32.050 --> 00:12:33.050
ear.

00:12:33.050 --> 00:12:36.889
It makes sense that Otto is close with the
maesters, because the maesters are based in

00:12:36.889 --> 00:12:38.930
the Hightower city of Oldtown.

00:12:38.930 --> 00:12:44.100
Otto even wears a chain on his neck similar
to a maester’s chain.

00:12:44.100 --> 00:12:51.130
So together, Otto and Mellos subtly manipulate
Viserys – saying yes there are good reasons

00:12:51.130 --> 00:12:56.410
to marry Laena Velaryon, but they also say
that it would anger Rhaenyra, and that it’s

00:12:56.410 --> 00:13:00.029
an insult to the memory of Viserys’ dead
wife.

00:13:00.029 --> 00:13:07.069
So without saying it directly, Otto and Mellos
pressure Viserys not to marry Laena.

00:13:07.069 --> 00:13:11.589
Viserys and Laena have an awkward walk of
courtship in the garden.

00:13:11.589 --> 00:13:15.180
Like Sansa’s awkward walks with Loras in
Game of Thrones.

00:13:15.180 --> 00:13:20.180
Laena and Viserys are both very uncomfortable
with this marriage proposal.

00:13:20.180 --> 00:13:24.980
Though age gaps in political marriages are
not uncommon in Westeros.

00:13:24.980 --> 00:13:29.450
Like, in the books, Sansa is twelve when she
marries Tyrion.

00:13:29.450 --> 00:13:33.060
And Daenerys was thirteen when she marries
Drogo.

00:13:33.060 --> 00:13:37.589
Girls are considered ready to have sex once
they have their first period – here Laena

00:13:37.589 --> 00:13:42.190
says she’s expected to have sex with Viserys
when she turns fourteen.

00:13:42.190 --> 00:13:48.019
The books emphasise the horror that Sansa
and Daenerys experience as child brides, and

00:13:48.019 --> 00:13:53.850
show the dangers of young pregnancies – in
this world, girls’ bodies are political

00:13:53.850 --> 00:14:00.100
objects, used to perpetuate bloodlines, just
as mens’ bodies are on battlefields.

00:14:00.100 --> 00:14:05.560
Laena is not interested in marriage – she’s
interested in dragons.

00:14:05.560 --> 00:14:11.050
She asks about Vhagar, the oldest and biggest
dragon in the world, ever since the death

00:14:11.050 --> 00:14:15.250
of Viserys’ dragon Balerion.

00:14:15.250 --> 00:14:21.199
Vhagar was the dragon of Queen Visenya Targaryen,
who conquered Westeros alongside Aegon.

00:14:21.199 --> 00:14:27.079
Then, Vhagar was ridden by Baelon Targaryen,
the father of Viserys and Daemon.

00:14:27.079 --> 00:14:32.760
These days, the old she-dragon has left King’s
Landing and retired to someplace on the east

00:14:32.760 --> 00:14:35.069
coast, as many older women do.

00:14:35.069 --> 00:14:40.730
And it’s kind of terrifying that the Targaryens
don’t know where their most dangerous weapon

00:14:40.730 --> 00:14:41.730
is.

00:14:41.730 --> 00:14:46.740
It’s yet another thing King Viserys is not
in control of.

00:14:46.740 --> 00:14:53.160
Laena says the workers at Spicetown sometimes
hear Vhagar’s song – Spicetown is a trading

00:14:53.160 --> 00:14:57.699
port on Driftmark, so maybe the Velaryons
could find Vhagar.

00:14:57.699 --> 00:15:01.759
Rhaenyra sees her father on a date with a
twelve-year-old.

00:15:01.759 --> 00:15:08.190
If Viserys remarries and has a son, that son
could replace Rhaenyra as heir to the Throne.

00:15:08.190 --> 00:15:13.010
Just like Rhaenys was replaced at the Harrenhal
Council when Viserys was made heir instead

00:15:13.010 --> 00:15:14.010
of her.

00:15:14.010 --> 00:15:19.999
Rhaenys says this is the order of things,
“Men would sooner put the realm to the torch”

00:15:19.999 --> 00:15:22.300
that see a woman on the Throne.

00:15:22.300 --> 00:15:27.500
In Game of Thrones we see how hard it is for
Daenerys and Cersei to hold power, though

00:15:27.500 --> 00:15:32.449
to be fair it is Daenerys and Cersei who torch
the realm, not the men.

00:15:32.449 --> 00:15:37.930
Rhaenys has mixed feelings for Rhaenyra – she
feels sympathy that Rhaenyra is facing the

00:15:37.930 --> 00:15:43.490
same obstacles she faced, but she also feels
a little jealousy, or spite, as though she

00:15:43.490 --> 00:15:46.610
doesn’t want Rhaenyra to succeed where Rhaenys
failed.

00:15:46.610 --> 00:15:47.882
According to the actor, Rhaenys wants to take
Rhaenyra down a peg.

00:15:47.882 --> 00:15:52.589
But Rhaenyra insists that she’ll become
queen, and will make a new order, a more fair

00:15:52.589 --> 00:15:54.269
political system.

00:15:54.269 --> 00:15:57.680
Like when Daenerys she’ll break the wheel.

00:15:57.680 --> 00:16:01.379
Will Rhaenyra succeed where Daenerys fails?

00:16:01.379 --> 00:16:05.800
We learn that Viserys’ brother, Prince Daemon,
has been living on Dragonstone for the last

00:16:05.800 --> 00:16:11.170
six months – despite the fact that Viserys
ordered Daemon to go to the Vale to his estranged

00:16:11.170 --> 00:16:12.920
wife Rhea Royce.

00:16:12.920 --> 00:16:17.529
Daemon took his gold cloaks to Dragonstone,
even though the gold cloaks are meant to be

00:16:17.529 --> 00:16:19.140
guarding King’s Landing.

00:16:19.140 --> 00:16:23.370
And now, Daemon does something even more provocative.

00:16:23.370 --> 00:16:28.550
He calls himself the rightful heir to the
Throne instead of Rhaenyra.

00:16:28.550 --> 00:16:33.980
And he says he’s gonna marry his lover Mysaria,
even though Daemon’s already married to

00:16:33.980 --> 00:16:35.329
Rhea Royce.

00:16:35.329 --> 00:16:41.269
The Targaryens and Valyrians have a history
of marrying multiple wives – Aegon the Conqueror

00:16:41.269 --> 00:16:44.800
married both his sisters Rhaenys and Visenya.

00:16:44.800 --> 00:16:50.160
But according to the Faith of the Seven, polygamy
is a sin – King Maegor went to war with

00:16:50.160 --> 00:16:55.709
the Faith when he married six wives, after
that disaster, the Targaryens stopped their

00:16:55.709 --> 00:16:57.589
polygamous marriages.

00:16:57.589 --> 00:17:03.139
If Daemon brings back that tradition he could
reignite this old conflict with the Faith.

00:17:03.139 --> 00:17:07.110
But Daemon also steals a dragon egg.

00:17:07.110 --> 00:17:12.040
Because traditionally, the Targaryens put
a dragon egg in the cradle of their babies

00:17:12.040 --> 00:17:17.800
so that the dragon hatchling bonds with the
baby – and Daemon says Mysaria is pregnant

00:17:17.800 --> 00:17:18.800
with his child.

00:17:18.800 --> 00:17:24.690
And the specific dragon egg that Daemon stole
is the egg that was going to be Prince Baelon’s,

00:17:24.690 --> 00:17:29.630
Viserys and Aemma’s baby that was gonna
be Viserys’ heir – Daemon’s “heir

00:17:29.630 --> 00:17:33.920
for a day” speech was what started his fight
with Viserys in the first place.

00:17:33.920 --> 00:17:41.270
So in one day, Daemon commits treason, blasphemy,
egg theft, and insults Viserys over his dead

00:17:41.270 --> 00:17:45.590
baby again – forcing the king to take action.

00:17:45.590 --> 00:17:51.680
Viserys says he’ll go and face Daemon himself,
but Otto says he can’t allow that, it’s

00:17:51.680 --> 00:17:52.680
too dangerous.

00:17:52.680 --> 00:17:57.270
Viserys is the king, but it often seems like
Otto is the one in charge.

00:17:57.270 --> 00:18:02.920
Later, Viserys says “I am your king”,
and in Game of Thrones Tywin says “Any man

00:18:02.920 --> 00:18:07.090
who must say, "I am the king" is no true king”.

00:18:07.090 --> 00:18:11.040
Otto goes to Dragonstone and tells Daemon
to surrender.

00:18:11.040 --> 00:18:14.430
But Daemon just asks where’s Viserys.

00:18:14.430 --> 00:18:19.520
The reason Daemon does all this is cause he
wants attention and acknowledgement from his

00:18:19.520 --> 00:18:20.520
brother.

00:18:20.520 --> 00:18:26.540
Daemon faces Criston Cole, the knight who
defeated him at the tournament last episode.

00:18:26.540 --> 00:18:32.250
Daemon calls Criston “Ser Crispin” instead,
just like in Game of Thrones when Jaime calls

00:18:32.250 --> 00:18:33.670
Dickon “Rickon”.

00:18:33.670 --> 00:18:41.350
Daemon has his fierce and freaky blood-red
dragon Caraxes, so Otto can’t defeat Daemon

00:18:41.350 --> 00:18:44.120
without a lot of dudes getting barbecued.

00:18:44.120 --> 00:18:47.570
But then Rhaenyra turns up on her dragon Syrax.

00:18:47.570 --> 00:18:53.340
With her dragon, Rhaenyra can’t be bossed
around by Otto any more – so she takes charge,

00:18:53.340 --> 00:18:55.330
and confronts Daemon.

00:18:55.330 --> 00:19:01.010
By calling himself heir to the Throne, Daemon
undermines Rhaenyra’s position as heir.

00:19:01.010 --> 00:19:05.120
Dragonstone itself is traditionally the seat
of the heir to the Throne.

00:19:05.120 --> 00:19:11.310
Rhaenyra dares Daemon to kill her and take
her place as heir – and it looks like Daemon

00:19:11.310 --> 00:19:16.200
thinks about it – but for all his violence
and chaos Daemon doesn’t want to kill his

00:19:16.200 --> 00:19:18.930
family, so Daemon gives up the egg.

00:19:18.930 --> 00:19:25.220
The dragon egg is kept in this hot container,
because dragon eggs seem to like heat.

00:19:25.220 --> 00:19:30.740
Daemon’s lover Mysaria is angry because
despite Daemon’s announcements, Mysaria

00:19:30.740 --> 00:19:35.920
wasn’t told that they would be married,
and Mysaria isn’t pregnant – she says

00:19:35.920 --> 00:19:37.770
she can’t get pregnant.

00:19:37.770 --> 00:19:43.250
Mysaria says that Daemon’s political games
might be fun for him, but they could easily

00:19:43.250 --> 00:19:45.250
get her killed.

00:19:45.250 --> 00:19:48.560
Men like Otto see Mysaria as a disposable
hoare.

00:19:48.560 --> 00:19:49.560
[Ironic, given how Otto is using Alicent].

00:19:49.560 --> 00:19:55.210
We saw in Game of Thrones how people like
Cersei and Tywin treat women they see as hoares.

00:19:55.210 --> 00:20:00.930
Mysaria says she’s been sold as property,
and lived in terror most her life – it’s

00:20:00.930 --> 00:20:07.090
a similar backstory to Melisandre’s in Game
of Thrones, who was also a slave in the east

00:20:07.090 --> 00:20:09.120
who learned to survive.

00:20:09.120 --> 00:20:14.710
we saw Melisandre with Stannis brooding on
Dragonstone, much like Mysaria and Daemon

00:20:14.710 --> 00:20:15.710
on Dragonstone.

00:20:15.710 --> 00:20:21.490
Like Daemon, Stannis also wanted the Throne
and the love of his older brother.

00:20:21.490 --> 00:20:26.470
Viserys goes to Lyonel Strong and asks for
unbiased advice.

00:20:26.470 --> 00:20:32.260
Viserys knows that Corlys and Otto are trying
to use him for their political gain.

00:20:32.260 --> 00:20:37.080
So he asks Lyonel for his outside opinion
on who Viserys should marry.

00:20:37.080 --> 00:20:41.120
Lyonel says he should marry Laena – cause
Corlys is an important ally, and they’ll

00:20:41.120 --> 00:20:43.740
need his ships if there’s war in the Stepstones.

00:20:43.740 --> 00:20:51.770
But Lyonel says that “Proud men don't like
having to look up” – while Lyonel looks

00:20:51.770 --> 00:20:53.600
up at Viserys.

00:20:53.600 --> 00:20:59.320
Lyonel is the Lord of Harrenhal, the biggest
castle in the realm and is leader of House

00:20:59.320 --> 00:21:02.700
Strong, “an ancient line of noble warriors”.

00:21:02.700 --> 00:21:08.540
Surely Lyonel is a proud man too – so what
are his ambitions?

00:21:08.540 --> 00:21:14.280
Viserys gets angry that Rhaenyra flew off
to Dragonstone without his permission.

00:21:14.280 --> 00:21:20.290
Viserys feels very protective of Rhaenyra
– maybe because his wife died, he’s terrified

00:21:20.290 --> 00:21:22.560
of losing his daughter too.

00:21:22.560 --> 00:21:28.320
But Rhaenyra points out she got results – she
got the dragon egg back without violence – and

00:21:28.320 --> 00:21:32.190
she wants to show Viserys her trust her in
her abilities.

00:21:32.190 --> 00:21:37.440
So Viserys acknowledges that he needs to let
Rhaenyra grow into an adult.

00:21:37.440 --> 00:21:42.400
Rhaenyra says she understands that as king,
Viserys needs to remarry and have more kids.

00:21:42.400 --> 00:21:47.870
So for the first time in months, Viserys and
Rhaenyra really connect emotionally – but

00:21:47.870 --> 00:21:52.950
there’s a misunderstanding here, because
Rhaenyra thinks Viserys is talking about marrying

00:21:52.950 --> 00:21:54.030
Laena Velaryon.

00:21:54.030 --> 00:22:00.380
But really, Viserys is thinking of marrying
Alicent.

00:22:00.380 --> 00:22:06.450
Alicent fixes Viserys’ broken dragon statue,
so maybe Viserys thinks Alicent can fix his

00:22:06.450 --> 00:22:11.880
broken family – or he just wants a wife
who supports his dorky hobbies.

00:22:11.880 --> 00:22:16.570
Or he’d just rather marry a fourteen year
old than a twelve year old.

00:22:16.570 --> 00:22:22.320
Either way, Viserys announces he’ll marry
Alicent Hightower.

00:22:22.320 --> 00:22:25.900
And this pisses off everybody except Otto.

00:22:25.900 --> 00:22:31.820
Corlys is furious because by rejecting Laena,
the Targaryens have rejected his family again

00:22:31.820 --> 00:22:32.820
just like Rhaenys was rejected at the Harrenhal
Council.

00:22:32.820 --> 00:22:37.740
Rhaenyra is upset because it’s weird that
her dad is marrying her best friend, and also

00:22:37.740 --> 00:22:42.590
cause Viserys and Alicent kept their relationship
secret from her.

00:22:42.590 --> 00:22:47.420
Alicent looks anxious about marrying this
old guy and becoming queen.

00:22:47.420 --> 00:22:51.310
And Daemon will be angry, because a child
of Viserys could push him further back in

00:22:51.310 --> 00:22:52.310
the line of succession.

00:22:52.310 --> 00:22:53.310
Viserys marrying Alicent is not necessarily
a bad idea – as king he’s gotta marry

00:22:53.310 --> 00:22:54.310
someone, and the Hightowers are powerful allies,
and Alicent can produce heirs sooner than

00:22:54.310 --> 00:22:57.600
Laena can – but Viserys’ failure to communicate
with Rhaenyra and to appease Corlys creates

00:22:57.600 --> 00:23:02.520
huge divisions at a time when House Targaryen
is already looking vulnerable.

00:23:02.520 --> 00:23:07.620
Daemon and Corlys get together on Driftmark,
the Velaryon island.

00:23:07.620 --> 00:23:13.510
Corlys’ home is decorated with maps and
skulls and a be-barnacled bust – artifacts

00:23:13.510 --> 00:23:15.920
from Corlys’ sea voyages.

00:23:15.920 --> 00:23:21.230
Corlys and Daemon are both angry at Viserys,
so they decide to do their own thing, and

00:23:21.230 --> 00:23:27.690
to attack the Crabfeeder – to end the threat
to Corlys’ ships, and to win glory for them

00:23:27.690 --> 00:23:28.690
both.

00:23:28.690 --> 00:23:32.900
Corlys says House Velaryon have always been
underdogs.

00:23:32.900 --> 00:23:38.280
Even back in Valyria, the Targaryens had dragons,
but the Velaryons didn’t, so they had to

00:23:38.280 --> 00:23:41.420
make their own power with their ships and
grit.

00:23:41.420 --> 00:23:48.280
Corlys is a self-made man because his voyages
around the world made his family rich.

00:23:48.280 --> 00:23:53.430
Corlys mentions building his seat by his own
strength – cause Corlys used his wealth

00:23:53.430 --> 00:23:57.340
to build a new castle on Driftmark, called
High Tide.

00:23:57.340 --> 00:24:02.580
He also mentions the Driftwood Throne, which
is the seat of the Lord of Driftmark.

00:24:02.580 --> 00:24:07.580
According to legend, the ancient Driftwood
Throne was given to the Velaryons by “the

00:24:07.580 --> 00:24:08.680
Merling King”.

00:24:08.680 --> 00:24:12.830
Corlys says that he and Daemon are “second
sons” who must prove their worth.

00:24:12.830 --> 00:24:20.590
Cause the laws of inheritance mean that firstborn
sons like Viserys inherit the lordships and

00:24:20.590 --> 00:24:21.740
lands.

00:24:21.740 --> 00:24:25.710
Second sons, like Daemon and Otto often inherit
nothing.

00:24:25.710 --> 00:24:28.950
So they’ve got to find their own place in
the world.

00:24:28.950 --> 00:24:33.380
Some second sons join the maesters, or the
Faith, or the Night’s Watch.

00:24:33.380 --> 00:24:38.270
Some become tournament knights or mercenaries
– there’s a whole mercenary group called

00:24:38.270 --> 00:24:44.030
the Second Sons who join Daenerys in Game
of Thrones. in the books, Oberyn Martell and

00:24:44.030 --> 00:24:47.220
later Tyrion join the Second Sons.

00:24:47.220 --> 00:24:52.680
Some second sons are jealous and resentful
of their big brothers – like Stannis with

00:24:52.680 --> 00:24:54.180
his brother Robert.

00:24:54.180 --> 00:25:00.450
Daemon is a classic example of a second son
who feels overshadowed by his brother.

00:25:00.450 --> 00:25:07.100
Corlys is not literally a second son as far
as we know – but House Velaryon has always

00:25:07.100 --> 00:25:10.580
been the second family in Westeros, they’re
the Valyrians who don’t have dragons, they’re

00:25:10.580 --> 00:25:14.410
always less powerful than the royal Targaryens.

00:25:14.410 --> 00:25:20.940
So Corlys and Daemon decide to prove themselves
by going to war with Craghas Crabfeeder.

00:25:20.940 --> 00:25:25.840
So in this episode, divisions deepen between
the most powerful people in the realm.

00:25:25.840 --> 00:25:26.840
Prince Daemon, Lord Corlys, and Princess Rhaenyra
all feel angry and rejected by the king, setting

00:25:26.840 --> 00:25:31.190
the stage for fiery conflicts in the future.

00:25:31.190 --> 00:25:37.410
